    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0272" n="202" xml:id="pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3305b: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to All Missions in Europe Except
                        Paris </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-26T18:00:00-05:00"
                            >November 26, 1918—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is of high importance that the American Embassy in Paris should be advised of
                    the political developments as they occur in the country to which you are
                    accredited. Accordingly you are instructed to telegraph to the American Embassy
                    in Paris for Col. House copies of your cable despatches to the Department when
                    in your judgment Paris should be so advised. At the end of each cable despatch
                    you should advise the Department whether Paris has been informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
